; need for large external capital (debt/equity) to fund required manufacturing or…; operational scaling failures (manufacturing capacity constraints) that prevent…"},{"claim":"EPS and net income growth demonstrate operational leverage: as high‑margin franchises scale…","helps":"eps diluted rose from 5.80 USD (FY 2023) to 11.71 USD (FY 2024) to 22.95 USD (FY 2025); net income increased from 5.24B USD (FY 2023) to 10.59B USD (FY 2024) to 20.64B USD (FY 2025)…","hurts":"large, value‑destroying acquisitions or equity raises increasing share count…; material margin compression from price or cost pressure so rising revenue fails…; regulatory fines or litigation expenses that hit net income and reduce…"}],"breaks_the_case":"A sustained, structural loss of exclusivity/pricing power for the company’s top‑selling new medicines (via rapid competitive approvals, payer exclusions or regulatory/safety constraints) that leads to secular revenue decline rather than a temporary slowdown.","full_case":"available via get_thesis"}}}]},"isError":false}}

